#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17b31ef7-a3d0-5315-8dbd-e92eafcce17f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order Differential Equation Using Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/id #uuid "c25573a9-f51a-5cf2-aa32-a343e96dd732" :question/math-academy-id "e-6612" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} - 4 \\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} + 5y = \\sin x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. The characteristic equation has roots\n\n$$\n\\lambda = 2 \\pm \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nso the complementary solution is\n\n$$\ny_c = e^{2x}(A\\cos{x} +B\\sin{x})\n$$\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $\\sin x$, and $\\sin x$ is not a term in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form\n\n$$\ny_c = \\alpha \\cos{x} + \\beta \\sin{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are constants to be determined.\n\n**Caution:** The terms of the complementary solution are $A e^{2x} \\cos x$ and $B e^{2x} \\sin x$. Although $\\sin x$ appears, $\\sin x$ is not itself a term because it is multiplied by $e^{2x}$.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy_{p}}{dx} &= - α\\sin x + β\\cos x, \\\\\n\\frac{d^{2}y_{p}}{dx^{2}} &= - α\\cos x - β\\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(- α\\cos x - β\\sin x) - 4(- α\\sin x + β\\cos x) + 5(α\\cos x + β\\sin x) &= \\sin x \\\\\n(4α - 4β)\\cos x + (4α + 4β)\\sin x &= \\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding terms on both sides should have the same coefficients. Equating the coefficients of like terms, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{4α - 4β = 0\\begin{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\cos x) \\\\ 4α + 4β = 1\\end{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\sin x)\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives\n\n$$\n\\alpha= \\beta = \\dfrac 1 8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = \\dfrac{1}{8} \\cos {x} + \\dfrac{1}{8} \\sin {x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= y_{c}(x) + y_{p}(x) \\\\\n&= e^{2x}(A\\cos x + B\\sin x) + \\frac{1}{8}\\cos x + \\frac{1}{8}\\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087546 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1292269f-5e99-5354-924d-824238118a8d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order ODE When the Right-Hand Side and the Complementary Solution are Dependent"}] :question/id #uuid "b11bf2d1-c79a-5308-bcda-109d217b14cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6613" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. The characteristic equation has roots\n\n$$\n\\lambda = \\pm 2 \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nso the complementary solution is\n\n$$\ny_c = A\\cos{2x} + B \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution $y_p(x)$.\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $4 \\sin 2x$, and $\\sin 2x$ is a term in the complementary solution. So, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\ny_p = x (\\alpha \\cos{2x} + \\beta \\sin{2x})\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are constants that are to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy_{p}}{dx} &= (α\\cos 2x + β\\sin 2x) + 2x(- α\\sin 2x + β\\cos 2x), \\\\\n\\frac{d^{2}y_{p}}{dx^{2}} &= 4(- α\\sin 2x + β\\cos 2x) + 4x(- α\\cos 2x - β\\sin 2x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4(- α\\sin 2x + β\\cos 2x) + 4x(- α\\cos 2x - β\\sin 2x) + 4x(α\\cos 2x + β\\sin 2x) &= 4\\sin 2x \\\\\n- 4α\\sin 2x + 4β\\cos 2x &= 4\\sin 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{4β = 0\\begin{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\cos 2x) \\\\ -4α = 4\\end{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\sin 2x)\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha = -1$ and $\\beta = 0$.\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = -x \\cos{2x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= y_{c} + y_{p} \\\\\n&= A\\cos 2x + B\\sin 2x - x\\cos 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087554 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c07e202-40b7-5508-af3d-6a272ed0cbc2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "a23b7e25-1876-5a71-a638-18b5d548bd16" :question/math-academy-id "e-6788" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x$\nhas the general solution\n$y(x) = A \\cos{2x} + B \\sin{2x} - x \\cos{2x}$,\nsolve the initial value problem\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x, \\qquad y(0) = 2, \\ \\ y'(0) = -3$." :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n$2|= A\\cos 0 + B\\sin 0 - 0\\cos 0; 2|= A$.\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n$y^{′}|=-2A\\sin 2x + 2B\\cos 2x - (\\cos 2x - 2x\\sin 2x); =-2A\\sin 2x + 2B\\cos 2x - \\cos 2x + 2x\\sin 2x$.\nSubstituting $y'(0)=-3$ into the derivative gives\n$-3|=-2A\\sin 0 + 2B\\cos 0 - \\cos 0 + 2(0)\\sin 0; - 3|= 2B - 1; - 2|= 2B; - 1|= B$.\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=-1$, we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny = 2\\cos 2x - \\sin 2x - x\\cos 2x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c07e202-40b7-5508-af3d-6a272ed0cbc2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94083d65-4a98-503f-99f6-7d2c346de080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\cos 3x - \\sin 3x + x\\cos 3x + x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085934} {:answer/id #uuid "97cb78d7-bbcb-59fb-843a-2ed2d7833ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 2\\cos 3x + \\sin 3x + 2x\\cos 3x + x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085935} {:answer/id #uuid "a1534329-1fba-515c-ae3c-f11f561e3ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\cos 3x - 4\\sin 3x + x\\cos 3x + 5x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085936} {:answer/id #uuid "a62fa116-32ac-5f1b-bf99-f912975f5d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\cos 3x - 2\\sin 3x + x\\cos 3x - x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085937} {:answer/id #uuid "a92cc537-cd9a-546c-9bb3-325b63bf005f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 2\\cos 3x + 3\\sin 3x + 4x\\cos 3x + x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97cb78d7-bbcb-59fb-843a-2ed2d7833ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 2\\cos 3x + \\sin 3x + 2x\\cos 3x + x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085935} :answer-field/id #uuid "976aa527-321c-5b0c-a9d3-b13424b4db15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085933}] :question/id #uuid "7a70227b-6237-55b5-b378-b7662770487e" :question/math-academy-id "q-64228" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$y^{″} + 9y = 6\\cos 3x - 12\\sin 3x, y(0) = 2, y^{′}(0) = 5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1292269f-5e99-5354-924d-824238118a8d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order ODE When the Right-Hand Side and the Complementary Solution are Dependent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91b3f5a8-3b2c-5755-bee0-fc30a055f06d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{p} = x\\cos 3x - x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085946} {:answer/id #uuid "bb060350-7550-5537-a3e7-466c038bf858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{p} =-x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085947} {:answer/id #uuid "1985efb7-2303-5654-9dc1-16a2e0f7f9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{p} = x\\cos 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085948} {:answer/id #uuid "60c2ee01-0268-55e7-95cd-0cdfe667451a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{p} = 2x\\cos 3x + 5x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085949} {:answer/id #uuid "76f7d593-532b-5f91-9f36-273628a8394f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{p} = x\\cos 3x + x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb060350-7550-5537-a3e7-466c038bf858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{p} =-x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085947} :answer-field/id #uuid "af993e0a-d970-5d1c-abe2-ed48d257b3e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085945}] :question/id #uuid "6bd36cb5-e3b7-5d05-9be7-a0cde384d7ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-64275" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 9y =-6\\cos 3x$\nhas the complementary function $y_{c}(x) = A\\cos 3x + B\\sin 3x$, find the particular solution $y_{p}(x)$ to this equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17b31ef7-a3d0-5315-8dbd-e92eafcce17f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order Differential Equation Using Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a46c4865-f0b4-5d4f-ba37-ce7f3fdc2cb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :a